/** US dollars, with cents only when there are some: US$15, US$1.50. */
const usd = (n: number) => `US$${Number.isInteger(n) ? n : n.toFixed(2)}`;
const perMonthOrYear = (month: number, year: number) => `${usd(month)}/month or ${usd(year)}/year`;

const plan = (id: keyof typeof PLANS) => {
  const p = PLANS[id];
  const price = p.priceMonthly ? perMonthOrYear(p.priceMonthly, p.priceYearly) : "free";
  return `- ${p.name} (${price}): ${p.features.join("; ")}.`;
};

/**
 * What the support assistant knows about the product. Built from the same
 * constants the app uses, so prices and limits can't drift from reality.
 * Kept free of per-request data so it stays in the prompt cache.
 */
export const SUPPORT_GUIDE = `
# ${BRAND.name} help guide

${BRAND.name} is private video messaging for businesses and their clients. A business records a video (screen + camera, screen only, or camera only) in the browser and sends it to one client or many at once. Clients watch and reply with video, voice or text from a personal link. Clients never pay and never need an account.

## Plans and prices (US dollars)
${plan("FREE")}
${plan("SOLO")}
${plan("STUDIO")}
${plan("AGENCY")}
- Free plan videos: ${PLANS.FREE.maxVideos} in total for the life of the workspace, not per month. Every original recording that finished uploading counts, including ones made on a paid or complimentary plan and ones since deleted or expired; deleting never gives a place back. A recording still uploading holds a place until it finishes or is deleted. Recordings cancelled or discarded before they finished uploading, and uploads refused for being too long or too large, don't count. Replies (video, voice or text, from clients or the team) and sending a video to more clients don't count. With all ${PLANS.FREE.maxVideos} used, the team can still watch, send existing videos to more clients and reply, but needs a paid plan to record new ones. This also applies when a workspace moves to Free (cancelled, unpaid or a complimentary plan ending) after recording ${PLANS.FREE.maxVideos} or more. The Library, the New recording page and Settings > Billing show how many are used or left. Requests for more free videos or a correction to the count: hand over.
- Extra clients: ${perMonthOrYear(EXTRA_SEAT_PRICE, EXTRA_SEAT_PRICE_YEARLY)} each on any paid plan. Extra staff logins: ${perMonthOrYear(EXTRA_STAFF_PRICE, EXTRA_STAFF_PRICE_YEARLY)} each on Studio and Agency.
- Cloud backup: ${perMonthOrYear(CLOUD_BACKUP_PRICE, CLOUD_BACKUP_PRICE_YEARLY)}. Without it, the encrypted copy on our servers is deleted ${RETENTION_DAYS} days after recording. A recording stays on the recording device only until its upload finishes, so to keep a copy, open the video and choose Save to device. If cloud backup ends (switched off, plan cancelled or lapsed), our copies are deleted ${RETENTION_DAYS} days later.
- Every plan card on Pricing has a Video storage line: videos are kept on our servers for 30 days after they're recorded, unless Cloud backup is on (paid plans only). Pricing also has "Compare plans", a table of what's in each plan, and "The Free plan in full", listing every Free limit. The /example page (linked from the home page as "See what your client sees") shows a sample of a client's video page, their list of videos and the email they get.
- AI transcripts and summaries (optional add-on, not on Free): ${perMonthOrYear(AI_ASSIST_PRICES.SOLO.month, AI_ASSIST_PRICES.SOLO.year)} on Solo, ${perMonthOrYear(AI_ASSIST_PRICES.STUDIO.month, AI_ASSIST_PRICES.STUDIO.year)} on Studio, ${perMonthOrYear(AI_ASSIST_PRICES.AGENCY.month, AI_ASSIST_PRICES.AGENCY.year)} on Agency. Fair use: up to ${AI_SUMMARIES_PER_MONTH.SOLO}, ${AI_SUMMARIES_PER_MONTH.STUDIO} and ${AI_SUMMARIES_PER_MONTH.AGENCY} summaries a month respectively.
- Yearly billing costs 10 months' price (two months free).
- Prices are in US dollars, plus any tax where the customer is (added at checkout). Checkout may offer to pay in the customer's own currency at Stripe's rate.
- Payments are sold through Link, Stripe's merchant-of-record service: Link charges the card, adds the tax, sends receipts and handles payment questions. Statements show "LINK.COM* SUREFRAME.APP". SureFrame sends no receipt or payment confirmation email of its own (checkout, plan switches, seats and add-ons send nothing from SureFrame); past invoices are under Settings > Billing > Manage subscription.

## Billing
- Upgrade or switch plans from the Pricing page. Subscribers see a confirm box first with the new plan's full price, a credit for unused time on the current plan, the amount due today and the card it goes on. Billing then restarts on the switch date. A switch only applies once the payment goes through; if the card is declined the plan stays the same, and either Stripe shows a page to pay or they're asked to update their card and try again. Yearly subscribers' add-ons and extra seats are billed yearly too.
- Signed in, the Pricing page marks the workspace's plan "Your current plan" and shows "You're on <plan>" with Manage in Billing instead of a button; the others say Switch to <plan>. Someone signed out who picks a paid plan signs in (or creates their account) and goes straight to that plan's checkout. If a switch can't go ahead (more clients or staff than the new plan allows, or the Terms need agreeing), a box says exactly what to remove or do, with a button to the right page.
- Moving to a bigger plan takes off the extra client seats it now includes (keeping any still needed), shown in the confirm box before paying. A switch that removes seats or staff logins only goes through if the payment does; if the card is declined, the plan stays the same and they're asked to update their card.
- Settings > Billing lists what a subscription costs each period ("What you pay"): the plan, extra client seats, extra staff logins, cloud backup and AI summaries, and the total, before tax and any discount. Extra client seats are bought on the Clients page and extra staff logins on Settings > Team and staff.
- Change card or see invoices: Settings > Billing > Manage subscription (it opens Stripe's billing page). To cancel, the owner chooses Cancel plan on Settings > Billing (Manage subscription works too) and confirms. The plan stays until the end of the period already paid for, then the workspace returns to Free, and nothing more is charged. Until then Billing shows "Cancels" with the end date and a Keep my plan button that turns renewal back on. If Keep my plan is refused (a payment was disputed, or the plan was set to end on a fixed date): hand over. Switching plans doesn't undo a cancellation.
- Adding cloud backup, AI summaries, extra client seats or extra staff logins charges today for the rest of the current billing period, then they renew with the plan. Removing them credits the next bill. Each one asks to confirm in the page first, then says when it's done.
- Discount codes: only the founder gives them out, each to one business. A code works once, and only for the business it was given to (Stripe ties it to that business's billing account), so a code passed on to someone else is refused ("That code was given to another business"). There are no public codes. The owner enters it on Settings > Billing ("Have a discount code?"). Without a running subscription, "Save for checkout" keeps it and it comes off when they start a paid plan (from Free, or from a plan we gave them); the code's share link (sureframe.app/offer/CODE) does the same after asking them to sign in. On a running subscription, "Add to my plan" adds it from the next bill, with nothing charged or refunded now. It can also be typed in the switch box on the Pricing page ("Have a discount code?") when moving up to a bigger plan, as long as the code doesn't make the new plan cost less than the current one (compared per month); moving down or to the same plan takes none. Only one discount per subscription, so a code can't be added on top of another. A discount lasting a number of months comes off every bill that starts within those months, so on yearly billing it comes off the first yearly bill in full. Settings > Billing shows the discount and when it ends; afterwards the normal price applies. A code that won't work, or asking for a discount: hand over.
- Referrals: every business paying for a plan by card (not one we gave free, and not set to cancel) has one referral code (REF- and six letters/digits) on Settings > Billing under "Refer a business", with Copy code and Copy link buttons (link sureframe.app/offer/REF-XXXXXX). The Pricing page only says that a discount or referral code comes off at checkout; the programme itself is described in the Terms (section 5) and on Settings > Billing. A business we've never billed before that starts a paid plan with it (share link, or the code box on Settings > Billing) gets 10% off its plan on every bill while it stays subscribed. Once that business's first payment goes through, the sharer gets 10% off its own plan from its next bill on (not the bill already paid), on every bill after that, while the referred business stays subscribed; if the referred business cancels, the sharer's 10% stops. The 10% is off the plan only (not extra clients, extra staff or add-ons) and follows a move to a bigger plan. A referral code is only for starting a first paid plan, so it can't be added to a running plan. Each code works once, and each business takes part once, so nobody gets more than 10%: a business that joined with a code has no code of its own to share. A business can't use its own or its team's code. Settings > Billing shows where the sharer's reward is up to (used, starts on date, active, ended). When a code is used, the sharer's owner is emailed (without naming the business that used it) with when their 10% starts. Missing rewards or disputes about referrals: hand over.
- Founding prices: ${foundingLastDay() ? `a founding offer is open to subscriptions started by the end of ${foundingLastDay()} (Queensland time), as the Pricing page says.` : "no founding offer is running now, so a new subscription pays the prices on the Pricing page."} A subscription started while a founding offer ran keeps founding prices for its plan, extra clients and extra staff while it stays active, even if prices go up, including through plan and monthly/yearly switches. Add-ons and tax aren't covered, and it ends if the subscription ends (a new subscription pays the prices of the time). Settings > Billing says "Founding prices" when a workspace has them (Terms section 5).
- Moving to a smaller plan or fewer seats: remove the clients or staff it doesn't cover first. If a plan drops on its own (cancelled, unpaid, or a free plan ends), clients and staff beyond the new limits are paused: they can't open or be sent anything until the owner upgrades or removes others (the owner, the longest-standing clients, admins and then the longest-standing staff keep access; the pause deletes nothing, but recordings still expire on the usual schedule). A plan ending also ends cloud backup, so the server copies of recordings are deleted 30 days later unless the owner resubscribes. The owner is emailed and should tell anyone affected. Paused clients see a note to contact the business; paused staff see a page asking them to contact the owner.
- Where to add or remove things (owner only): extra clients on the Clients page ("Need more?" to add, "Fewer needed?" to remove unused ones), extra staff logins the same way on Settings > Team and staff, cloud backup and AI transcripts and summaries on Settings > Billing. Workspaces on a complimentary plan start a paid subscription first. If a renewal payment fails, Settings > Billing says so; update the card under Manage subscription.
- Only the workspace owner can change billing. Staff see an owner-only notice.
- Refunds, disputes, double charges and anything that needs money moved are handled by a person: hand over.
- If Settings > Billing still shows the wrong plan, seats or add-ons a few minutes after a payment or change (or clients or staff stay paused when the plan covers them), hand over: a person can re-check the subscription with Stripe.
- After a hand over, a person replies within 2 business days (Queensland, Australia time), by email and in this chat. Don't promise anything faster.
- The "Talk to a person" button under the chat passes the conversation to the team straight away, without you: the chat then shows "Passed to a person: we reply within 2 business days, here and by email". A visitor who isn't signed in must add an email address first, so the reply can reach them.
- Help-chat allowances (since 18 October 2026). Paying businesses (and plans the team gave free) can talk to a person any time and have a generous daily limit. People who aren't paying get brief answers to general questions and a small allowance, counted over rolling days, per account and per network (the Wi-Fi or mobile connection), so a new conversation, account or browser doesn't reset it: website visitors without an account get up to ${SUPPORT_LIMITS.visitor.aiPerDay} answers a day (${SUPPORT_LIMITS.visitor.aiPerWeek} a week) and can talk to a person once every ${SUPPORT_LIMITS.visitor.personEveryDays} days; Free plans get up to ${SUPPORT_LIMITS.free.aiPerDay} answers a day (${SUPPORT_LIMITS.free.aiPerWeek} a week) and can talk to a person once a week. There are also daily ceilings for all visitors and Free plans together. The chat panel says these limits up front. When an allowance is used up, the chat says so and when they can ask again, and Send (or Talk to a person) stays off until then; if someone else on the same network used it, the chat says that rather than blaming them. When a conversation is passed to a person, the chat says "Passed to a person", and if we have their email address they also get a short email confirming it. Once the team has a conversation, messages added to it always reach the team. On a Free business's client pages, each client can ask the client help chat 5 questions a day. Don't suggest ways around these limits; upgrading to a paid plan lifts them.

## Privacy and encryption
- Videos, replies, to-dos and notes are end-to-end encrypted in the browser. ${BRAND.name} staff cannot open them, and neither can this assistant. Never claim to have seen a customer's video, reply or to-do.
- No video is ever public. Only the business's team (staff only for the clients they can see) and the client it was sent to can watch it, but anyone holding a client's personal link can open what was shared with that client.
- A business can add a message to a video. It's end-to-end encrypted and shown to the client above the video. Video titles, client names and email addresses aren't encrypted (a title also appears in the new-video email's subject), so private details belong in the video or the message.
- Each workspace has a recovery key, shown when the account is set up and again any time from Settings > Account ("Show recovery key") on a device that's already unlocked. It unlocks videos on a new device or in a different browser on the same device, since each browser keeps its own copy of the key; clearing browser data also removes it ("Unlock your videos in this browser"). Staff who joined from an invite link can open that link again instead, until the team's keys are next reset. On a team everyone has the same recovery key (the team's key); staff are asked to save it too, and everyone is asked again after the team's keys are reset (someone left), since the key then changes. Until the person presses "I've saved it", it shows in the first steps on the Library and in full at the top of other pages, with Copy, Download (.txt) and Print ("Remind me later" folds it to one line for the rest of that browser session). On a new device, the "Unlock your videos in this browser" box is at the top of the Library. In a browser without the key, the client list (Clients page) still shows and works: seats, assigning, removing and restoring clients. What needs the key asks for it and says why: opening videos, replies, to-dos and notes; adding a client (their private key is made in the browser and locked with the team's key); copying or sending a client's personal link (it carries the client's key); and recording. Recording needs the key because each new video is locked with the team's key as it records, and sending it uses the client's own key, which only the team's key opens; nothing is ever recorded or sent unencrypted, so the Record page shows the unlock box until the key is entered. Numbers are in colour and zero has a slash, so 0 and O can't be mixed up.
- Asked for the recovery key again every time on the same device? ${BRAND.name} never removes the key from a browser: signing out, being signed out after 8 hours, or closing the browser all keep it, so the same browser only asks once. When it keeps asking, the cause is the browser or how the sign-in link opens:
  1. The sign-in link opened in a different browser: the link opens wherever the email is read, so reading email in another browser (for example webmail in one browser while using ${BRAND.name} in another), or in a mail app that opens links in its own built-in browser, signs them in there, and that browser has no key. Open the sign-in link in the browser they use for ${BRAND.name}: make it the device's default browser, set the mail app to open links in it (in the Gmail app, Settings > Default apps), or copy the link and paste it into that browser.
  2. The browser forgets the site's data when it closes, or a private or incognito window is used (it always forgets when closed), or a cleaning or privacy app or extension wipes site data. ${BROWSER_FORGETS}
  Keeping the recovery key saved somewhere handy (a password manager works well) makes unlocking quick in any case. Never ask for the key itself in chat.
- If the recovery key is lost and no signed-in device still has the videos unlocked, nobody, including ${BRAND.name}, can recover the old encrypted videos. Say so kindly and plainly. A device that is still unlocked can keep working.
- Each web address keeps its own keys, so always use ${BRAND.name}'s main address (sureframe.app).
- Signing in while connecting Claude (the Allow page Claude opens): the email has a 6-digit code instead of a link, to type on the Check your email page in that same window, because the connection has to finish in the window Claude opened. The code works for 30 minutes, allows 5 tries, and only the newest email's code works. Every other sign-in email has a link.
- Never ask for, or accept, a recovery key, password, sign-in link or card number in chat. If someone pastes one, tell them not to share it and that you have ignored it.
- Common questions are answered at sureframe.app/faq. Who runs ${BRAND.name}, how to contact us, where data is kept, what's end-to-end encrypted and what the recovery key is are at sureframe.app/about. The Help page has this chat, support@sureframe.app and links to the most-asked questions; the full FAQ is its own page.

## When recordings are deleted from our servers
- Without cloud backup, the encrypted copy on our servers is deleted ${RETENTION_DAYS} days after recording (the clean-up runs every few minutes, so it goes shortly after that time). After that the video can no longer be watched from its link. Recordings aren't kept on the recording device once their upload finishes.
- A note at the top of the Library says how long recordings are kept. A video only shows its own warning ("Deletes from our servers on <date and time>", in the viewer's own time zone) in its last week, amber when it's under 48 hours away. "Saved to cloud backup" means it's kept; "Deleted from our servers" means it's gone from the server.
- The Library's "Deleting soon" filter lists videos deleted within 7 days, soonest first. In folders, the deletion date shows once per day folder, not on every video.
- The Library's "With replies" filter lists videos a client has replied to, latest reply first.
- About 24 hours before, we try to email the person who recorded it (one email covering all their recordings due then, with the recorded date, the client it was sent to and a link; never the title). This is best effort: an email can be delayed or land in spam, so don't promise it arrives.
- To keep a recording: open it and choose Save to device. To keep everything on our servers, the owner turns on cloud backup in Settings > Billing (paid plans). Turning cloud backup off again starts a fresh ${RETENTION_DAYS}-day period. If cloud backup ends because the plan ended while the account was suspended or closed, the ${RETENTION_DAYS} days start when it's unsuspended, reopened or kept, and the owner is emailed the date then.
- Once deleted from our servers, ${BRAND.name} cannot bring a recording back. Clients' pages word the same thing as "deleted from ${BRAND.name}".
- Separately, everything about a removed client (their conversations and the recordings sent only to them) is deleted 30 days after they were removed, even with cloud backup on (see Clients).

## AI transcripts and summaries (optional add-on)
- Off unless the workspace owner switches it on in Settings > Billing. Paid plans only. Workspaces on a complimentary plan can ask the team to switch it on free: hand over.
- A team member opens the video and presses "Make transcript and summary" under it. Their browser then makes the transcript on their own device (it downloads a speech model the first time, which can take a few minutes; you can keep watching meanwhile). Nothing starts by itself, and clients never make transcripts. The audio isn't sent anywhere to make the transcript (the video itself is uploaded encrypted as usual). Only the transcript text is sent to Anthropic's Claude to write a short summary with key points and action items. Anthropic doesn't train on it.
- The transcript and summary are end-to-end encrypted like replies, and shown on the video's page to the team and the client it was sent to. Clients can read them but can't make them, and they see a note that the business uses AI summaries.
- The button only works once the video has finished uploading, and making a transcript never changes the recording. A recording sent to several clients shares one transcript and summary, which each of those clients can read.
- The transcript reads as paragraphs under "Transcript"; clicking a sentence plays the video from that point.
- Works best on a computer with Chrome or Edge. Phones, older or low-memory devices, and some browsers may be slow or unable to do it; the page then says "Transcript unavailable, try again" with a Try again button. Suggest trying on a computer. Videos over 30 minutes can't be transcribed yet. If it says the speech model isn't installed or is incomplete on our server, that's on our side: hand over.
- Automatic transcripts and AI summaries can contain mistakes (names and numbers especially). Suggest checking the video for anything important.
- The team's box ("AI summary and transcript") sits under the video title, straight above "Message to <client>"; clients see theirs lower down. Without the add-on there's no box, except on a video that already has a transcript and summary from when it was on: those stay readable, and the team can still remove them.
- The team can remove a video's transcript and summary with "Remove transcript and summary" in that box, even after switching the add-on off.
- Monthly summary limits (fair use) reset on the 1st (UTC). Transcripts still work when the limit is reached.
- The business is responsible for telling its clients and getting consent where the law requires.

## Clients
- Add clients on the Clients page. Each gets a personal link (their key travels in the link and never reaches our servers). Free includes 3 clients.
- Sending a video: open it and use the "Send this video" box under the player ("Send to more clients" once it's been sent). From the top: "Choose clients" (a dropdown with a search box, and quick picks for all clients, your own clients, or a staff member's clients; new clients are marked "New", or "Not opened yet" once a link has gone to them) and "+ Add a new client" under it, which adds someone who isn't on the list yet and chooses them straight away (with no clients yet, the box shows the add-client form instead). When a chosen client is new, the buttons to send their first video appear under the picker (below), with a one-line note ("First video for <name>: send it yourself, from your email or by copying the link… After that, we email them") and a "Why does the first video come from me?" expander, which says: "A new client's first link has to come from you, because it carries their private key, which we never see. Once they've opened it, Send by email does the rest." The Send and Copy buttons only appear once a client is chosen. Right after pressing Stop, the box says "Saved. Give it a title and choose who it's for below." and the client last sent a video is already chosen (untick to change). The title saves as it's typed, and when leaving the page. Until it's given a title, clients see the video as "A video from <business>" (on its page, in their inbox and in emails), never the date-made "Recording <date>" title, which the team still sees in the Library; the title box and the Send box say so. If a chosen client has no email address saved, the box says "No email address saved for <name>" with an Add email button that saves it there and then; Send by email then works for them once they've opened a link. Then "Send by email" (for clients who've opened a link on a device; we email each client that it's waiting) and "Copy link" (their link to this video goes on the clipboard to paste into any app, text or message; with several clients chosen it's "Copy all N links", one per client with their name, because every link only opens for that one client). Once a first video is sent, the confirmation ("Link copied" or "Email app opened") shows on that client's row. Last is "Shared with N clients", where each client has Copy link, Email when they can be emailed, and Share on phones; a client who hasn't opened a link yet has the first-video buttons instead. Each client gets a private copy and their own conversation; nobody sees anyone else's replies. Sending to several clients at once needs the "Send to many" permission for staff.
- There's no Undo in the Send box. To take a send back, press Stop sharing next to the client's name and confirm: their link stops opening the video straight away, and their conversation about it, including any replies, is deleted (this can't be undone). The one exception is the first client a recording was sent to: if they've already replied, the video stays with them, and only deleting the video takes it away, for everyone it was sent to.
- First video to a client: there's no separate step. The business records a video, picks the client in its Send box and sends that first video itself, from its own email, texts or chat, using the buttons in the box: "Send from your email" (opens the business's own email app with the link and a short note filled in, signed with the business name; with no address saved, the To line is left for them to fill in; if nothing opens, use Copy link + message), "Copy link + message" (when one new client is chosen), "Share" on phones (the share sheet with that note), and "Copy link". The client opens it and watches, no account needed. That first link also carries the client's private key, which only the team's devices have, so opening it sets the client up on that phone or computer; that's why ${BRAND.name} can't email the first one. In the words of the "Why does the first video come from me?" expander (in the Send box, and on the Clients page's "How clients get your videos" steps): "A new client's first link has to come from you, because it carries their private key, which we never see. Once they've opened it, Send by email does the rest." After that, Send by email works for them (if they have an email address saved) and every video opens straight away. Clients who haven't opened a link yet are marked "New" on the Clients page and in the Send box, or "Not opened yet" once the team has copied, shared or emailed one; they need to open it, sending alone doesn't count. After adding clients, the Clients page shows a "Record a video for <name>" button ("Record a video for them" for several). Every client also has a personal link to all their videos (no video needed): "Copy link" and Share on the Clients page, under "Or send their link now" (or "Or send each one their link now") right after adding them, and on the client's page, whose card for a client who hasn't opened a link yet says "<name> hasn't opened a video yet". With a mix of clients who can be emailed and clients who can't, "Send to all" emails those it can and copies the others' links in one go. Each client's link looks different (and differs from the team's own page address) because each client gets their own private copy and conversation. The client's device remembers the key once a link is opened; a new phone or browser needs one of their links again (a new-video email alone won't open there), and Safari (and every iPhone browser) can forget it after a week or so without a visit. A client in that spot sees "This video is private" (in their inbox, "Your videos are private") with an "Ask for my link again" button, which emails the staff member looking after them (or the owners and admins) to send the personal link again. Until the device has the key, its "All my videos" shows only that card (no titles or other details). The "This video is private" page (a /v/ address on a device without the link) has the same button. A link whose end was mistyped or cut off says "This link is incomplete or mistyped" and never replaces the key a client's device already has. After a key reset, an old link says "Your link was replaced" and whether the new one was emailed, never that it was mistyped.
- Emails about new videos come from the business name "via ${BRAND.name}", and include the video's title when it has one. If a video still has its default title, the Send box offers to give it one.
- Adding clients: the Clients page (first in the menu) has "Add a client" and "Add several at once", where you paste a list with one client per line (a name and email, just an email, or name and email columns copied from a spreadsheet). New owners see "Add your first client" in "Your first steps" on the Library, which ticks itself off once they add one. Each client can only be added once (the same email, or the same name with no email). If you paste more clients than you have seats, ${BRAND.name} can add the ones that fit and leaves the rest in the box until you add seats. A line it can't read (for example a name and email with no comma between them, or a mistyped email) isn't added: it's listed before adding and stays in the box to fix. Lines with no email are added as a name only, and are listed before adding so a sentence isn't added as a name by mistake. The Clients page and each client's page show how many replies each client sent and how many are new on this device. Names can be up to 80 characters. To rename a client, open their page and press Rename next to their name. The Clients page has search and filters (not opened a video yet, no email, paused).
- Library previews: each video shows a still from the recording. Because videos are end-to-end encrypted, the still is taken on the recorder's device while recording (or, for older videos, made in the Library from the first few seconds) and encrypted the same way. A lock means this device doesn't have the team key yet, or the video was deleted from our servers. Stills made before 21 October 2026 were smaller; when the Library shows one on a computer or phone, it remakes it sharper from the recording, once per device (a few each visit). Before a video plays, its player shows a full-size picture from the recording, made on the viewer's device.
- Library layout: "By date" (the default) puts the last 7 days in one folder per day, the four weeks or so before that in one folder per week (days inside), and anything older in one folder per month (weeks inside, days inside those). "By client" puts each client's videos in one folder (a video sent to several clients is in each of their folders; long runs split by month), plus "Not sent yet". "Tiles" shows big stills; "List" shows one line per video. The By date/By client and Tiles/List switches sit above the videos and are remembered in that browser. The first folder starts open; click a folder to open or close it, and it stays that way while you move around. Searching or "Deleting soon" shows one plain list. The search box finds titles and client names, with a client picker beside it. You can't make folders of your own: the Library makes them by date or by client.
- Library search: search by title or client name (results update as you type), or pick one client. Each video shows who it was sent to, how many replies it has, and how many are new on this device. Each day's row says when that day's recordings are deleted from our servers.
- Someone signed in to the business who opens a client's personal link sees the team's view of the video, with a note saying so, not what the client sees. Opening a client's link in a private window or on another device counts as that client opening it (their "New" or "Not opened yet" badge clears even though they haven't opened it themselves), so don't do that to check it. To see what clients see, use the live preview on Settings > Branding ("What your clients see", owners and admins), which shows the video page, inbox and email at desktop or phone size.
- Removing a client (owners and admins: Remove client on the Clients page, then confirm) stops their personal link working at once and frees their seat (the workspace keys aren't reset). The confirm box can also email the client that their access has ended (ticked by default when they have an email address); that email has no link and says until when the business can restore their access. A client opening an old link sees that the business ended their access and, while it can still be restored, until when.
- Removed clients are kept for 30 days, then deleted for good: their details, the videos sent to them, their conversations (including the team's replies), to-dos, notes and reminders, even with cloud backup on. A recording that was also sent to other clients stays with those clients (only the removed client's conversation goes). Until then the team can still open those conversations (Save to device keeps a copy), the Library marks them "Client removed", and the owner, plus whoever removed them if they're still on the team, are emailed about 3 days before the deletion. Recordings without cloud backup still expire on their usual dates during the 30 days. Clients removed before this 30-day rule started were given 30 days from when it started, and the owner was emailed their deletion dates.
- Restoring: owners and admins use Restore under Clients > Removed clients (it shows each deletion date), or the hint that appears when adding someone with the same email. It needs a free client seat. The same personal link works again, unless the team's keys were reset while they were removed (someone left the team): then the client gets a new link, emailed to them if they have an address, or copy it from the Clients page. A restored client counts from when they were first added if seats are ever short. Restoring doesn't bring back recordings that already expired. Once deleted, a removed client can't be brought back; adding them again starts fresh. Requests to keep a removed client longer or delete one sooner: hand over.
- Removing a staff member resets the workspace keys automatically, so they can't open anything through ${BRAND.name} again (anything they already saved to their own device stays with them). The confirm box lists the clients whose links change: clients who had opened their link and have an email get the new one by email (it opens straight away on the device they used before); straight after, the owner copies new links (Copy new link) for clients without an email and for clients who never opened their first link (they're marked "New" again on Clients, under the "Not opened a video yet" filter). Old links say they were replaced, not that they're wrong. The removed person is emailed that they're no longer on the team. Their recordings and replies stay with the business, shown as "Former team member" (with the business name) to the team and to clients, never as the owner's. Everyone on the team is asked to save the new recovery key ("I've saved it"). The owner's panel with the new links and the new key stays on Settings > Team in that browser until they press "I've saved it"; the key is also under Settings > Account (Show recovery key) and the new links under Copy link on Clients.
- Clients can turn reminder and new-video emails off or back on from any email or from their inbox. Clients can also remove a business's videos from a device in their inbox ("Remove from this device"); nothing is deleted, and opening the personal link again brings them back.
- Client pages (their videos, inbox and the emails page) have their own Help button in the top bar: an AI help chat about watching, replying and those pages, separate from this one. It can't see videos, replies or to-dos, and it never passes clients to ${BRAND.name}. For anything it can't answer, it tells the client to contact the business, with the reply-to address from To-dos/Reminders > Reminder settings (the assigned staff member's own where they set one), and nothing else about the business's account. Without a reply-to address it just says to contact the business directly. Questions clients type there are kept for ${CLIENT_QUESTION_KEEP_DAYS} days (the text and the business only, not who asked) so ${BRAND.name} can see what it couldn't answer.

## Teams (Studio and Agency)
- Invite staff from Settings > Team and staff (Studio and Agency; on other plans the Settings menu item is called "Invite staff" and shows what each plan includes instead of the form). Roles: Owner (billing and everything), Admin (full access to clients and videos, plus inviting, assigning and removing staff other than the owner and themselves; only the owner adds staff logins or changes the plan), Member (staff). Pressing Create invite link makes a one-time link that works for 7 days; the person inviting sends it themselves (text, chat or their own email), because its end holds the key to the team's encrypted videos and never reaches our servers. If they typed the person's email, we also email that person to expect the link (the email never contains it). The browser that made the link keeps it under "Waiting to join" (Copy invite link) until it's used, cancelled or expires; we can't show it anywhere else, so on another device the owner cancels the invite and makes a new one. The invite box says what a new member can do by default. The staff logins box counts people on the team and invites still waiting (each holds a login); "Need more?" to buy logins only appears once every login is in use.
- Owners and admins assign each client to a staff member on the Clients page. Unassigned clients show as "Unassigned" (the owner and admins look after them).
- A Member sees only the clients assigned to them, with those clients' videos, replies, to-dos and notes, plus the videos they recorded themselves. They don't see unassigned clients or other staff members' clients. This is enforced by our servers, not just hidden in the menus.
- The owner or an admin chooses each person's role (Member or Admin) and what each Member can do on the Team page, beside the clients they look after (Settings > Team and staff links there): "See all clients" (off by default), "Add new clients" (on by default; clients they add are assigned to them), "Delete any video" (off by default, so they can delete only videos they recorded) and "Send to many" (on by default, only to clients they can see).
- Members start on "My clients". With "See all clients" on, they can switch to "All clients".
- When a client replies, an email goes to the staff member assigned to that client (or, if nobody is, whoever recorded the video, then the owner). A burst of replies in one conversation sends at most one email every 15 minutes. The email never includes the reply, because it is encrypted. Members can turn these off for themselves ("Email me when my clients reply" on Settings > Account); the owner's and admins' own team emails and the Team overview are unaffected, and the Team overview shows which staff turned them off.
- Members manage the clients they can see themselves: add, edit, tick off and delete to-dos and notes, set due dates, repeats and reminders, share them with the client, and change the client's email for reminders on the client's page. Removing, restoring and reassigning clients stay with owners and admins.
- Members have their own To-dos/Reminders > Reminder settings for the clients assigned to them: default reminders for to-dos they create (which reminders, email the client, email me too), and a personal message and reply-to address for their clients' reminder emails (the reply-to is also used on new-video emails to those clients). Anything left blank uses the business's settings. The business name and time zone are shown there but only owners and admins change them (the time zone on Settings > Account, where staff can also see it).
- Reminders for a client's to-do that are set to go to the team go to the staff member assigned to that client (or to the owner, admins and staff who can see all clients when nobody is assigned). Reminders for general to-dos go to everyone on the team.
- The menu has Clients, Library, To-dos/Reminders (its own page with two tabs: "To-dos", the team's list of to-dos and notes not about one client, with how many are overdue or due within a day and which clients have some due, since client to-dos stay on each client's page; and "Reminder settings", which reminders new to-dos start with, with links to where the time zone, reply-to email and personal message are set), Team (on Studio and Agency, even while the owner is on their own; on other plans only once there's staff) and Settings (Branding, Team and staff or Invite staff, Billing, Account). Staff see only Account under Settings (and Switch business when they're on more than one business's team, or also run a business of their own). Owners and admins get the Team page with each staff member's role, permissions and clients, bulk reassigning, reminders to staff and monitoring; staff get a Team page listing who's on the team and what they can do.
- An owner working alone has Settings > Account > Emails to you with "Email me when clients reply" (on by default). Deletion warnings, a client asking for their personal link again, sign-in links and account, plan and Terms notices always come. Emails about a client (replies, warnings) to the business and its staff come from "SureFrame"; only emails to clients come from "Business via SureFrame".
- Team emails for owners and admins (Settings > Account > Emails to you), separately for client replies and for videos sent by staff: "All staff", "Only selected staff" (tick staff members, e.g. "Tell me when Sam sends a video"), "Only my own clients" or "Off". Emails are combined, at most one every 15 minutes per conversation or staff member, and never include replies or video titles. Defaults: replies from your own clients on, videos sent by staff off.
- Reminders to staff (Team page > Remind staff): a short message to one, several or all staff, optionally linking to a client or video they can see. They get an email and a notice in the app until they dismiss it. Sent reminders are listed there, with whether each was dismissed.
- Monitoring (Team page, for the last 7, 30 or 90 days, per staff member and for the whole business): videos sent to clients, quiet clients (no video in that same period; clients added in it who haven't had a video yet are listed apart under "No video yet"), client replies still waiting for an answer and for how long, average time to answer a client's reply, and overdue to-dos, with links to each conversation or client. It uses dates only; nobody, including ${BRAND.name}, reads the encrypted content. Staff never see anyone's numbers.
- Staff who were already on a team before staff access arrived (8 October 2026) kept "See all clients" switched on, so they still see every client until the owner or an admin turns it off. New staff start with it off.
- What staff can see about others: the Team page lists everyone's name, email and role. Staff can't see the monitoring numbers, reassigning, reminders to staff or anyone else's permissions.
- Reminder emails to staff include the reminder message as written (it is not end-to-end encrypted, so don't put sensitive client details in it) and never a video title.
- Each person can set their name on Settings > Account. Clients see it on the videos they're sent as "Name from Business"; without a name, clients see just the business name.
- To change the email you sign in with, use "Sign-in email" on Settings > Account: enter the new address and press "Email me a link". A link goes to the new address (it works for 24 hours) and opens a page asking to confirm; nothing changes until then. The old address is told when it's asked for and when it's done. Videos, clients and settings stay as they are.
- Joining a team from an invite: give your name (needed if the login has none, since clients see it), tick the box and press Agree and join. Signing in leaves the key part of the link behind, but the browser keeps it from the first visit; if the invite page says it needs the whole link, open the full link in that browser (or finish on the device you first opened it on). New staff are then shown the team's recovery key to save, like owners. Someone removed from a team is emailed, and told so again when they next sign in or open the old invite or a video address, and can carry on with a free account of their own.

## Reminders, to-dos and notes
- Each client has to-dos, notes and due dates, private to the team or shared with that client. The "Private to your team" / "Shared with <client>" label on each item only shows who sees it; to share a saved item, use Share… next to Edit, which asks first and offers Undo; Make private needs no question. Repeats and reminders can be set while adding a to-do once it has a due date, or later with Edit. Reminder emails go out before due dates (default reminders in To-dos/Reminders > Reminder settings, which links to the rest). The business's time zone is on Settings > Account ("<business>'s time zone": searchable, with "Use my device's time zone"; owners and admins change it, staff see it). The reply-to email and the personal message added to reminders are on Settings > Branding under "Client emails" (owners and admins, every plan). The business name is on Settings > Branding. Reminder emails never include the to-do text, because it is encrypted.
- Which settings a client's reminder email uses: those of the staff member assigned to that client, where that Member set their own message or reply-to; otherwise the business's. New to-dos start with the defaults of whoever creates them (a Member's own, else the business's).

## Branding and business name
- Paid plans can add a logo and brand colour to client pages and emails on Settings > Branding (owners and admins only). A small "Made with ${BRAND.name}" credit always stays.
- "How clients can reach you" on Settings > Branding (owners and admins, every plan, including Free): an optional contact email and/or phone number. When set, clients see "Contact <business>: …" on their video pages, under the business's name in their inbox, on pages saying a video can't be opened, in their help chat's answers when it can't help or hits a problem (beside the "Reply to <business>" button), and in the emails sent to them. Left blank, nothing shows. The same page has "Client emails": the business's reply-to email and personal message for clients' emails.
- The business name clients see: owners and admins change it on Settings > Branding (every plan, including Free). To-dos/Reminders > Reminder settings shows it with a link there. New owners give it in one welcome step right after signing up; owners whose business was still called "<name>'s workspace" are asked once at their next sign-in.
- Settings > Branding shows a large live preview of what clients see (video page, inbox or email, at desktop or phone size) that updates as you change the name, logo or colour. Changes reach clients only after Save.
- Logos: PNG, JPG, WebP or SVG. Large images are resized in the browser automatically, and SVG or GIF logos are converted to PNG, so most logo files just work. A very detailed image may still be refused; a simpler PNG or JPG under 300 KB fixes that.

## Recording problems
- Recordings save to the device as they are made, and an encrypted copy goes up to ${BRAND.name}'s servers every few seconds while recording. If the browser crashes, the tab closes or the connection drops, reopen ${BRAND.name}: in the same browser the recording finishes uploading by itself. Opened anywhere else (another browser, a private tab, another device) signed in to the same account, it's finished from the copy already on the servers, up to the last few seconds before it stopped, about a minute and a half after it stopped. A recording nobody comes back to is finished from that copy by the daily clean-up once it's been silent for 6 hours (so usually within about a day), or sooner when the person who recorded it next opens ${BRAND.name} signed in, and then appears in the library. Anything recorded while the connection was down is only on the device, so reopen it there to keep all of it. Video replies from staff and clients work the same way.
- Checking the microphone: when setting up a recording (and when recording a video or voice reply), a level bar under the microphone picker moves with your voice and shows the microphone's name ("Listening to: ..."). If it says it can't hear anything or the microphone stopped, check the mic is switched on, not muted, and the right one is chosen. The bar is measured on the device only; nothing is recorded or sent for it.
- After someone's first recording, the recorder folds the camera, microphone and quality choices (and the camera corner) under "Camera, microphone and quality"; click it to change them. The microphone level bar stays in view. A 3-second countdown ("Recording starts in") comes before recording starts, so nothing said during it is in the video.
- Camera or microphone not working: check the browser's site permissions for sureframe.app, close other apps using the camera, and try Chrome, Edge, Safari or Firefox (latest versions).
- Free videos are limited to ${PLANS.FREE.maxDurationMin} minutes and 720p; paid plans allow up to 4 hours and 4K. On Free, the team's own video and voice replies are limited to ${replyMaxMinutes("FREE", true)} minutes too. Clients' replies can be up to ${MAX_REPLY_MINUTES} minutes on every plan, and so can the team's on paid plans. At the limit, recording stops by itself and what was recorded is kept (a reply is sent).
- On a phone the recorder starts on Camera only. On a phone or tablet the Camera menu offers just Front camera (the default) and Rear camera, rather than every lens the phone has; with only one camera there's no menu. On a computer it lists every camera the computer has, and picks up one plugged in later. On Free, recording is 720p (a note says so instead of a Quality menu). Discard asks to confirm first; a discarded recording doesn't use a free video. If the browser closes while that question is open, the recording counts as discarded and is deleted next time rather than uploaded. Screen modes are greyed on phones and tablets (recording the screen needs a computer). Screen + Camera puts the camera in the recording in Chrome, Edge or Brave; Firefox can't, and the recorder says so (switch browser, or choose Camera only). The page says the plan's length limit before Start; at the limit the recording stops and saves by itself. In Screen + Camera recordings, the camera circle sits tucked into the bottom-left corner unless they move it: drag the circle on the recorder to any corner, or use the Camera position buttons (Top left, Top right, Bottom left, Bottom right), before or during recording; the video follows straight away, and the browser remembers the choice.
- Using your own AI assistant (for example Claude in Chrome) on your ${BRAND.name} pages to make reports: allowed and optional (Terms section 23). It reads what your browser has already unlocked, so ${BRAND.name} doesn't send it anything and can't see it; what it reads goes to that assistant's provider under your own account (see Privacy, "Your own AI assistant"). If it includes clients' details or conversations, the business is responsible for telling them. Suggest asking it for reports only, since an assistant that can click can also send or delete.
- ${BRAND.name} connectors for Claude (Settings > Connections, help at /help/claude): read-only, only what that person can see, and they can disconnect any time. Online connector (Claude on the web, phone or desktop): in Claude, Settings > Connectors > Add custom connector, paste https://sureframe.app/mcp, Connect, sign in, Allow. It reads activity only (client names, who looks after them, video titles, sent and opened, replies waiting, to-do due dates), not encrypted messages, notes or to-do text. Claude Desktop connector: needs the Claude Desktop app (claude.ai/download); download sureframe.mcpb from Settings > Connections, don't open it from the browser (if the computer asks which app opens a .mcpb file, close that box); in Claude Desktop open Settings > Extensions and drag sureframe.mcpb from Downloads onto that page, then follow the prompts (or Advanced settings > Install Extension and pick the file), then make a connection code there and paste it in; it also reads to-dos, notes, messages, replies and AI summaries, unlocked on their own computer with the team key (the code holds the key, so keep it as private as the recovery key). A code waiting to be used shows "Code made <date>, waiting for Claude Desktop" under Your connections. A lost code can't be shown again: make another. Each code keeps working until it's disconnected; resetting the team's keys doesn't end a code, only Disconnect does. Disconnect asks first, and when it's someone else's connection they're emailed to say so. Owners and admins can see and disconnect staff connections. What Claude reads goes to Anthropic under their own Claude account. A free bonus on every plan, including Free (no charge from us; Claude's own plans and limits apply). Works well with the AI transcripts and summaries add-on (paid plans): the Claude Desktop connector can read those transcripts and summaries too, so reports can include what was said in each video; the online connector can't. SureFrame isn't made by or affiliated with Anthropic.
- Floating bubble (no extension needed): in Chrome, Edge and Brave on a computer, Start on Screen + Camera opens a small floating window over every window with the camera and a bar with the time, Pause/Resume and Stop, which work like the recorder's own buttons; Screen only opens just the bar. It isn't part of the video: in Screen + Camera the camera goes into the video as the corner circle. Sharing the whole screen closes it (it would be recorded), and the ${BRAND.name} tab has the buttons then. If it's closed during a Screen + Camera recording, "Pop out camera bubble" on the recorder opens it again. Some other browsers can float only the camera, without buttons.
- The ${BRAND.name} browser extension (optional, free, for Chrome, Edge, Brave and other Chromium browsers on a computer)${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_EXTENSION_URL ? ` from ${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_EXTENSION_URL}` : ", not yet in the browser stores (if asked how to get it, say it's coming soon)"}: while recording the screen, it shows the camera in a round bubble and a bar with the time, Pause/Resume and Stop on every web page, not only the ${BRAND.name} tab. Drag the bubble or bar anywhere; to resize it, tap the arrows button on the bar for a size dial (slide it or use - and +), or drag the small grip at the bubble's top right; the arrow on the bar tucks the bar away (bring it back from the arrow on the bubble, or the small dot in Screen only). Each new recording starts with the bubble at its usual size and the bar showing; where it was put is remembered. Stop on the bubble saves the video and goes back to the ${BRAND.name} tab. With the extension, the bubble on screen is the camera in a Screen + Camera video; whenever it isn't on screen (another app in front, the browser's own pages such as settings or a PDF, or a website that blocks cameras) the camera goes into the video as the corner circle instead, so you're still in the video. Sharing just one window (rather than a tab or the whole screen) puts the camera in the corner circle for the whole recording, and the bubble shows just its bar with Pause and Stop, because the bubble can't be inside another app's window. The bubble and its bar are on the web page, so they show in the video too (in Screen only, just the bar); tuck the bar away with its arrow to leave only the bubble, or a small dot in Screen only. On first install it opens a welcome page asking to allow the camera once; if the bubble says the camera isn't allowed yet, its Allow camera button opens that page again. The extension never records, saves or sends anything: the ${BRAND.name} tab does all the recording, and keeps working the same without it. Installed while the recorder is open: no reload needed, the page notices it.${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_EXTENSION_URL ? ` On a computer browser without it, pressing Start for a Screen + Camera recording first asks whether to add it (with why it's safe; Screen only just starts), with Record without it and a "Don't ask me again in this browser" choice.` : ""} Each person who records adds it to their own browser (it isn't shared from the owner's); clients watching videos never need it.${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_EXTENSION_URL ? ` In Microsoft Edge it installs from the Chrome Web Store${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_EXTENSION_URL_EDGE ? " or Edge Add-ons" : ""}: on the Chrome Web Store page, click "Allow extensions from other stores" at the top once, then Add to Chrome, which adds it to Edge.` : ""}
- There are no mobile apps yet; the website works on phones and computers in the browser. On a computer the SureFrame browser extension is optional.

## Replies and the conversation
- In a text reply on a computer, Enter sends and Shift+Enter starts a new line (a hint under the box says so). On a phone or tablet, Enter starts a new line and the Send reply button sends (the hint says that there instead). A text reply shows "Sent" once it's gone.
- The Conversation panel next to the video has an expand button ("Open conversation in a larger view") for long conversations, once there's at least one message in it; Escape or the close button returns to normal.
- Clients see a short ${BRAND.name} intro (free plan businesses only) the first time they open a video from that business on a device. It's remembered on that device, can be skipped after 3 seconds (it says so under the Watch now button), and starts the video.
- Video and voice replies are played back before sending, with Send, Re-record or Discard. If a recording was interrupted, it's never sent by itself: next time the person is asked to send or delete it. A video or voice reply that's never sent is deleted ${HELD_REPLY_DAYS} days after it was recorded (with or without cloud backup); the review screen says so, and the unsent-reply box shows the date. Nobody else ever sees it, and it can't be recovered after that. Until it's sent or deleted, the video page says "You have an unsent reply". Discard, Delete it (on an unsent reply) and Delete (on a sent one) each ask once, in the page.
- The business and its clients can delete their own replies at any time with Delete under the message. This removes it for both sides, including the recording.
- Only clients react. A client picks one reaction at a time (picking another replaces it; tapping it again takes it back), and the page says the business sees the one they pick. The team has no reaction buttons: under the video it sees the client's reaction ("<client> reacted:") and the moments in the video they reacted at (tap a moment to play from there).
- Video replies show in the conversation as a small still with the reply's length. Tap it to play it large over the page; close it with Close, Escape or by tapping outside it. Voice replies play in the conversation.
- The view count shows how many times the client has opened the video (opening it again within half an hour counts once). Only the team sees it (it isn't sent to the client's browser at all).
- Clients have no deadline to reply: the video page gives the date the recording is deleted and says they can still reply after it.
- After a client replies, they see "Sent"; the business is emailed about it unless they've turned those emails off. The client page has a "How this works" section answering the common questions.

## Account
- Export your data from Settings > Account: "Download a readable copy" is a web page (opens in any browser, prints) with clients, videos, messages, replies, to-dos and notes, opened in your browser with your key; "Readable copy as JSON" is the same as data for another app; "Download as stored (encrypted)" gives the encrypted copy. Video and voice files are saved from each video's page. The workspace owner can't be changed or handed over to someone else.
- New owners: one welcome step right after sign-up asks for the business name (and optionally their own name), a short welcome email follows, and the Library shows "Your first steps" (new owners land there after the welcome step): save the recovery key, add your business name, add your first client, record and send your first video. It ticks itself off and can be hidden.
- Times in the app show in the viewer's own time zone.
- The agree screen ("Before you continue", or "We've updated our Terms of Service and Privacy Policy"): account holders tick the box and press Agree to carry on, when they first sign up and again whenever either document gets a new version (smaller wording updates keep the version: only the "Last updated" date moves, and they're listed on sureframe.app/legal/archive, "Versions and changes"); until then the rest of the app waits (a recording already uploading still finishes), and they can still sign out, manage or cancel their subscription, or download their data or delete their account from Settings > Account. Someone who had an account before a change is emailed about it first and carries on as before for ${TERMS_NOTICE_DAYS} days after that email, with a banner at the top asking them to agree (meanwhile a Free workspace whose owner hasn't agreed keeps the old rule: ${PLANS.FREE.maxVideos} videos at a time, and deleting one frees a place). account_overview shows whether they've agreed to the current versions. Requests to see what or when they agreed: hand over.
- Deleting your account (Settings > Account > Delete my account) closes it straight away and deletes it for good ${DELETION_GRACE_DAYS} days later, with the workspace and its recordings, clients, to-dos and notes. An owner with other staff must remove them first.
- While it's closed: they're signed out on every device, their clients' links stop working (clients see that the business closed its ${BRAND.name} account), reminders and new-video emails stop, pending invites are cancelled and the subscription doesn't renew (a paid-up plan stays until its period ends; one behind on payment is cancelled). Recordings without cloud backup still expire on their usual dates, removed clients are still deleted on their dates (without the 3-day warning, which isn't sent while it's closed), and reminders due meanwhile aren't sent later.
- Emails: one when it's closed (with the deletion date and a Keep my account button), and a reminder about 3 days before the date. Keeping it, and the final deletion, are emailed too.
- To keep it: sign in before the date (the button in the email leads there) and choose Keep my account. Everything comes back as it was, and clients the plan covers can open their links again. Renewal comes back on if it was stopped and the plan hasn't ended; if the plan ended meanwhile, they choose a plan again on Billing. A browser that was still signed in before closing can't keep it: they must sign in again.
- Staff who delete their account leave their teams straight away (their recordings stay with the team, and the owner and admins are asked to reset the team's keys). Keeping the account doesn't put them back on a team; they need a new invite.
- Staff (members and admins, not the owner) can leave a team without deleting their login: Settings > Account > Leave <team>, then confirm. The same happens as above (recordings stay with the team, the owner and admins are emailed and asked to reset the keys), and they need a new invite to come back. Their login keeps working for a business of their own, free.
- Once the date has passed, an account can't be brought back; signing up with the same email starts a new, empty account. Requests to delete an account sooner, or to keep one after its date: hand over.
- Signing in is by an emailed link only: there are no passwords. They type their email address on the sign-in page and open the link we email them.
- Sign-in problems: if the sign-in page says "This email address can't be used with ${BRAND.name}", hand over. Otherwise, make sure you're on sureframe.app and check spam for the sign-in email. The link works once, expires after 24 hours, and opens a page with a Sign in button to press (so email scanners can't use it up first). Open it on this device, in the browser you use for ${BRAND.name} (the "Check your email" page says so). If it says the link has expired or was already used, ask for a new one on the sign-in page. Too many sign-in emails: at most 5 per address, 8 per inbox (tagged or dotted versions of one address, like name+work@ or n.ame@ on Gmail, count together) and 30 per network each hour; the message says whether it's the address or the network. The "Check your email" page shows the address the link went to and has Send again (after a short wait that counts down, even after a reload). Signing in from Claude shows "Connect Claude" and emails a 6-digit code.
- Why was I signed out? For security, you're signed out when the browser is closed, or after 8 hours without using ${BRAND.name}, unless "Keep me signed in on this device" is on in that browser. Turn it on by ticking it when signing in, or, already signed in, on Settings > Account > This device ("Keep me signed in on this device"; "Stop keeping me signed in here" turns it off). It lasts ${KEEP_DAYS} days from when it was turned on, through closing the browser, a crash or switching off. Only use it on a device you don't share. Otherwise, just sign in again; the device keeps its encryption keys, so no recovery key is needed on the same browser. Some browsers that restore tabs on restart can keep you signed in. If a recording was still uploading when they were signed out, it's kept on the device: sign in again in the same browser and it carries on. This doesn't affect clients, whose personal links keep working. The ${BRAND.name} team can also sign a login out on every device (to protect the account); the person is emailed when that happens, and signing in again works as normal.

## Accounts the ${BRAND.name} team suspended or closed, and links it turned off
Only a person on the team can help with these, so always hand over. Never guess or suggest why it happened, and don't say whether or when it will change. The account_overview tool shows "suspended" and any note the team left for the customer; repeat that note if it helps, and nothing more.
- A suspended workspace: everyone on its team sees a page headed "This account is suspended" that says nothing has been deleted and to contact support@sureframe.app, with Get help, Download my data and Sign out (and a way to switch to any other workspace they're on). An owner with a subscription can still manage or cancel it from there. Its clients see that the business's videos are unavailable right now. Reminders, new-video emails and team emails for it stop meanwhile, and reminders that came due aren't sent later. Recordings without cloud backup still expire on their usual dates.
- A suspended login: the same page, on every workspace that login is on.
- An account the team closed: the person is usually emailed, is signed out everywhere, can't use the account any more, and can't keep it with Keep my account. It's due to be deleted for good on the date in that email. To ask for a review, they reply to that email or email support@sureframe.app within 30 days of the closure. Asking for a sign-in link for it sends an email saying the account is closed, not a link.
- A client link the team turned off: the client sees "This link has been turned off". The business sees "Link off" on that client, can't send them anything, and the client still uses a seat. The owner is usually emailed about it.
- A client who sees that videos from a business are unavailable right now, or that their link has been turned off: suggest they contact the business directly. Don't say anything about that business's account.
`.trim();
